# OpenRouter Rules

OpenRouter is used **only** as an internal peak-hour transport for DeepSeek and
Z.AI models that have OpenRouter twins in `config.openRouterTwins`. Cursor
aliases map to direct providers; the gateway reroutes to OR upstream IDs during
that provider's peak hours when an OpenRouter key is configured.

## HARD RULE: OpenRouter is peak-only

OpenRouter may **only** be used while the **equivalent real provider** is in peak
billing (`peakNow` in `peakguard.go`; `DISCURSIVE_FORCE_PEAK` counts as peak).
At all other times every path uses the real provider's real model:

- Peak reroute → `applyPeakReroute` + `config.OpenRouterTwinFor` (same-model twin)
- Subagent/router downgrades → `config.SmallModelFor(provider)` (never cross-provider)
- Compressor → request provider's small model (OR twin during that provider's peak)
- No sticky fallback, no Z.AI→DeepSeek overflow, no 429 cross-provider fallback

Enforcement:
1. Peak mapping: `applyPeakReroute` / `openRouterModelFor` in `peakguard.go`;
   twins in `config/providers.go` (`openRouterTwins`).
2. Send-time guard: `isPeakAllowedOpenRouter` corrects off-peak OR ids back to
   real models; logs at ERROR.
3. Tests: `TestOpenRouterOnlyDuringPeak` in `peakguard_test.go`.

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| OpenRouter charged outside peak | Hardcoded OR id at call site | Route peak swaps through `applyPeakReroute`/`OpenRouterTwinFor`; never hardcode OR ids |
| `openrouter_guard: off-peak OpenRouter usage blocked` | Producer emitted OR model off-peak | Fix producer to use real model off-peak; guard is last line of defense |

## Models

| Upstream id | Real model | Provider |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731` | `deepseek-v4-flash` | DeepSeek |
| `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813` | `deepseek-v4-pro` | DeepSeek |
| `z-ai/glm-5.3` | `glm-5.3[1m]` | Z.AI |
| `z-ai/glm-4.7` | `glm-4.7` | Z.AI |

Peak reroute mapping (non-downgraded traffic only; big vs small via `config.IsBigModel`):
- `deepseek-v4-pro` → `deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813`
- `deepseek-v4-flash` → `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731`
- `glm-5.3` / `glm-5.3[1m]` → `z-ai/glm-5.3`
- `glm-4.7` → `z-ai/glm-4.7`
- Moonshot, Thaura: no peak reroute

Subagent/router downgrades stay on the same provider's small model. OR is not used
for downgrades off-peak; on peak, `applyPeakReroute` may swap the routed model to
its OR twin if one exists.

## API key

- Key field: `openRouterKeyEncrypted` in `config.AppSettings`
- Set via: `discursive set --openrouter-key <key>` or `--openrouter-key` flag on `init`
- Retrieved via: `settings.GetOpenRouterKey(dataRoot)` in gateway/server.go
- OpenRouter is optional — if no key is configured, peak traffic falls through to the direct provider (pay peak), zero downtime

